plotsalot (Python package)
https://github.com/joshuamyers22/plotsalot
Copyright (c) 2026 Joshua Myers, MIT License

Credit: plotsalot is the earlier Python adaptation of ggstatsplot. inferplot
takes several design ideas from it (the analyze/render split, frozen typed
results, keyword-only allowlisted signatures, explicit subject IDs, seeded
randomness recorded in results, and an R oracle with pinned versions and hashed
fixtures). Its frozen ggstatsplot 1.1.1 outputs supply known answers in
tools/reference/stats_reference.py. No plotsalot source code is included.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Datasets in oracle/datasets/

mtcars, iris, ToothGrowth, PlantGrowth, morley and sleep are exported from R's
built-in datasets package. bugs_long and Titanic_full are exported from
ggstatsplot (MIT, notice above). Files named edge_*.csv were written for this
project.
